senses
  entry
    definition "an occurrence of thorough mixing"
    id oewn-07390005-n
    partOfSpeech n
  entry
    definition "a new word formed by joining two others and combining their meanings"
    examples ("‘smog’ is a blend of ‘smoke’ and ‘fog’" "‘motel’ is a portmanteau word made by combining ‘motor’ and ‘hotel’" "‘brunch’ is a well-known portmanteau")
    id oewn-06299307-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms ("portmanteau word" portmanteau)
  entry
    definition "the act of blending components together thoroughly"
    id oewn-00381504-n
    partOfSpeech n
    synonyms (blending)
  entry
    definition "combine into one"
    examples ("blend the nuts and raisins together" "he blends in with the crowd" "We don't intermingle much")
    id oewn-01465097-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (intermix immingle intermingle)
  entry
    definition "blend or harmonize"
    examples ("This flavor will blend with those in your dish" "This sofa won't go with the chairs")
    id oewn-02706315-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (go "blend in")
  entry
    definition "mix together different elements"
    examples ("The colors blend well")
    id oewn-00395719-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (flux mix conflate commingle immix fuse coalesce meld combine merge)
